 \subsubsection{Dynamic Interactive Hyperlink Attribution and Epistemic Negative Containment}
 Table~\ref{tab:citation_eval} (Panel~B) profiles the explainable attribution mechanics across the 350-benchmark suite:
 \begin{itemize}
-    \item \textbf{Interactive Hyperlinked Attribution:} In accordance with Section~\ref{subsubsec:xai-provenance}, Full TERRA dynamically formats referenced opinions as interactive relative markdown links. Across benchmark completions, TERRA emitted $\mathbf{\TerraTotalMarkdownLinks}$ interactive links. Empirical auditing against the 20,000-case EEG index confirms that $\mathbf{\TerraResolvedMarkdownLinks/\TerraTotalMarkdownLinks}$ links ($\mathbf{\TerraMarkdownLinkResolutionRate}$) resolve directly to authentic opinion nodes, with $\mathbf{\TerraMarkdownLinkFidelityRate}$ semantic title-to-node fidelity (including authentic historical aliases such as the \textit{Slaughter-House Cases} dynamically resolving to its formal reporter caption \textit{Butchers' Benevolent Ass'n}, \texttt{83\_0036-01}). The remaining $\TerraBrokenMarkdownLinks$ exceptions sum exactly to $1{,}042 - 1{,}036 = 6$, comprising $\TerraBrokenNotProvidedLinks$ instances of \texttt{/case/not\_provided} emitted on unindexed statutory or procedural references (queries~B026 and~B075) and $\TerraBrokenUnindexedCorpusLinks$ instances where valid external case citations fell outside the 20,000-opinion indexed corpus (\textit{Sipuel v. Board of Regents}, \texttt{332\_0631-01} in queries~B010 and~B012; and \textit{Palko v. Connecticut}, \texttt{302\_0319-01} in query~B035), with zero fabricated phantom decisions. In stark contrast, all four baseline architectures emit \textbf{zero} interactive hyperlinks (\BaselinesMarkdownLinks), leaving their citations unlinked and unverifiable without manual docket lookups.
-    \item \textbf{Out-of-Corpus Negative Probe Containment (Category C):} On the $N=75$ unanswerable negative probes, under the formal piecewise precision formulation (where emitting zero citations constitutes safe epistemic silence, scored as $1.00$, while hallucinating citations is scored as $0.00$), Flat Vector RAG suffered severe context bleed, hallucinating $\CatCFlatEmittedCitations$ spurious case citations across unanswerable queries ($\CatCFlatCitationPrecision$ precision). In contrast, Full TERRA achieved $\mathbf{\CatCTerraCitationPrecision}$ precision, emitting only $\CatCTerraEmittedCitations$ citations across all 75 queries ($72/75$ clean refusals), confirming that NLI entailment gating successfully suppresses citation hallucination on out-of-domain inquiries.
+    \item \textbf{Interactive Hyperlinked Attribution:} In accordance with Section~\ref{subsubsec:xai-provenance}, Full TERRA dynamically formats referenced opinions as interactive relative markdown links. Across benchmark completions, TERRA emitted $\mathbf{\TerraTotalMarkdownLinks}$ interactive links. Empirical auditing against the 20,000-case EEG index confirms that $\mathbf{\TerraResolvedMarkdownLinks/\TerraTotalMarkdownLinks}$ links ($\mathbf{\TerraMarkdownLinkResolutionRate}$) resolve directly to authentic opinion nodes, with $\mathbf{\TerraMarkdownLinkFidelityRate}$ semantic title-to-node fidelity (including authentic historical aliases such as the \textit{Slaughter-House Cases} dynamically resolving to its formal reporter caption \textit{Butchers' Benevolent Ass'n}, \texttt{83\_0036-01}). The remaining $\TerraBrokenMarkdownLinks$ links do not resolve as written: three carry page-padding errors in the identifiers of cases that are in the corpus (e.g.\ \texttt{301\_001-01} for \texttt{301\_0001-01}, \textit{NLRB v. Jones \& Laughlin}; queries~B073 and~D038), and one is a bare \texttt{/case/118} path (query~B075). In stark contrast, all four baseline architectures emit \textbf{zero} interactive hyperlinks (\BaselinesMarkdownLinks), leaving their citations unlinked and unverifiable without manual docket lookups.
+    \item \textbf{Out-of-Corpus Negative Probe Containment (Category C):} On the $N=75$ unanswerable negative probes, under the formal piecewise precision formulation (where emitting zero citations constitutes safe epistemic silence, scored as $1.00$, while hallucinating citations is scored as $0.00$), Flat Vector RAG suffered severe context bleed, hallucinating $\CatCFlatEmittedCitations$ spurious case citations across unanswerable queries ($\CatCFlatCitationPrecision$ precision). In contrast, Full TERRA achieved $\mathbf{\CatCTerraCitationPrecision}$ precision, emitting $\CatCTerraEmittedCitations$ citations across all 75 queries ($\CatCTerraCleanRefusals$ clean refusals). In the deployed run, 74 of these 75 probes had no retrieved context, so this containment reflects refusal on empty retrieval rather than entailment grading of retrieved evidence.
